NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want the tool to return a draft. The tool has no model result yet."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" inside the tool. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" function to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPServer"},{"type":"text","value":". Give "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".server()"},{"type":"text","value":" the type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MCPToolContext"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" type-checks."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport type { MCPToolContext } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst draftNote = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'draft_note',\n  description: 'Draft a short note about a topic',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    topic: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server<MCPToolContext>(async (args, ctx) => {\n  const draft = await ctx.context.sample({\n    messages: [\n      {\n        role: 'user',\n        content: `Write a short note about ${args.topic}.`,\n      },\n    ],\n  })\n\n  if (typeof draft !== 'string') {\n    throw new Error('The sample result is not text.')\n  }\n\n  return draft\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'notes',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [draftNote],\n  sample: async (request) => {\n    const first = request.messages[0]\n    const content = first === undefined ? '' : first.content\n    return `Draft: ${content}`\n  },\n})\n\nexport function handleMcp(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" is a method on the context of the tool. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" function is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(request) => Promise<unknown>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"spec-2025-and-spec-2026","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec 2025 and spec 2026"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec 2025"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" asks the MCP client. It does not call the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec 2026"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" calls the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" function. It does not ask the client."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec 2026 with no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" throws an Error. The message names "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"draft_note"},{"type":"text","value":" with a topic. The tool result is the draft text."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"spec-2025-and-spec-2026","text":"Spec 2025 and spec 2026","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want the tool to return a draft. The tool has no model result yet.\n\nCall `ctx.context.sample` inside the tool. Pass a `sample` function to `createMCPServer`. Give `.server()` the type `MCPToolContext`, so `ctx.context.sample` type-checks.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport type { MCPToolContext } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst draftNote = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'draft_note',\n  description: 'Draft a short note about a topic',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    topic: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server<MCPToolContext>(async (args, ctx) => {\n  const draft = await ctx.context.sample({\n    messages: [\n      {\n        role: 'user',\n        content: `Write a short note about ${args.topic}.`,\n      },\n    ],\n  })\n\n  if (typeof draft !== 'string') {\n    throw new Error('The sample result is not text.')\n  }\n\n  return draft\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'notes',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [draftNote],\n  sample: async (request) => {\n    const first = request.messages[0]\n    const content = first === undefined ? '' : first.content\n    return `Draft: ${content}`\n  },\n})\n\nexport function handleMcp(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}\n```\n\n`ctx.context.sample` is a method on the context of the tool. The `sample` function is `(request) => Promise<unknown>`.\n\n## Spec 2025 and spec 2026\n\n| Spec | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Spec 2025 | `ctx.context.sample` asks the MCP client. It does not call the `sample` function. |\n| Spec 2026 | `ctx.context.sample` calls the `sample` function. It does not ask the client. |\n| Spec 2026 with no `sample` | `ctx.context.sample` throws an Error. The message names `sample`. |\n\nCall `draft_note` with a topic. The tool result is the draft text.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Draft Text from a Tool\nid: mcp-server-sample\norder: 13\ndescription: \"Call ctx.context.sample from an MCP server tool so the tool can return a draft.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mcp\n  - model context protocol\n  - createMCPServer\n  - sample\n  - ctx.context.sample\n  - mcp server\n  - MCPToolContext\n---\n\nYou want the tool to return a draft. The tool has no model result yet.\n\nCall `ctx.context.sample` inside the tool. Pass a `sample` function to `createMCPServer`. Give `.server()` the type `MCPToolContext`, so `ctx.context.sample` type-checks.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport type { MCPToolContext } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst draftNote = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'draft_note',\n  description: 'Draft a short note about a topic',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    topic: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server<MCPToolContext>(async (args, ctx) => {\n  const draft = await ctx.context.sample({\n    messages: [\n      {\n        role: 'user',\n        content: `Write a short note about ${args.topic}.`,\n      },\n    ],\n  })\n\n  if (typeof draft !== 'string') {\n    throw new Error('The sample result is not text.')\n  }\n\n  return draft\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'notes',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [draftNote],\n  sample: async (request) => {\n    const first = request.messages[0]\n    const content = first === undefined ? '' : first.content\n    return `Draft: ${content}`\n  },\n})\n\nexport function handleMcp(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}\n```\n\n`ctx.context.sample` is a method on the context of the tool. The `sample` function is `(request) => Promise<unknown>`.\n\n## Spec 2025 and spec 2026\n\n| Spec | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Spec 2025 | `ctx.context.sample` asks the MCP client. It does not call the `sample` function. |\n| Spec 2026 | `ctx.context.sample` calls the `sample` function. It does not ask the client. |\n| Spec 2026 with no `sample` | `ctx.context.sample` throws an Error. The message names `sample`. |\n\nCall `draft_note` with a topic. The tool result is the draft text.\n"}
